  "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"kevinrhaas\"} -->\n_Requested by **Kevin** \u00b7 [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01XPwihxLZTCL4xqRww9mX5v?thread=cmsg_01XPwihxLZTCL4xqRww9mX5vVZSUUy7wNkhEMsiofJcUAa)_\n\n## What\n\nThe owner asked, 2026-11-03: *\"when the bridge was down did it really have a peak in the center like this, it seems very odd to me that would be the case\"*. In 1835, the closed draw of the Dearborn Street drawbridge rose 1.2 m to a ridge at mid-river (T-2375, PR 1512: `draw_profile: peaked`, `draw_rise_m: 1.2`). It now lies level with the approaches.\n\n## Why the picture is not followed\n\n- The rise came from one composition drawn twice: Braunhold's plate in Andreas 1884 p. 631 and the Baker-Co engraving. They share the same schooner, lighthouse and viewpoint, so they are not two witnesses. Both were made 40+ years after the bridge was chopped up in 1839.\n- No text gives a rise. Andreas says the draw was \"hoisted\" by \"gallows\" frames, and Moses & Kirkland (1895) p. 95 call it \"a double draw\".\n- 1.2 m over a 9.14 m leaf is a grade of about 1 in 7.6 each way, with the leaves' joint at its crest, on the town's main team crossing.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `data/structures/dearborn_street_drawbridge.json`: `draw_profile` flat, `draw_rise_m` 0. Both are reconstructed and argued in their notes, with the T-2375 reading kept as history.\n- Bridge GLB and its web derivative rebuilt, along with the sidecar and source-use backlinks.\n- `bridge_timber_params.walk_surface_profile`: a deck with a draw now states its profile even when level, so `placement.walk_surface_profile` stays carried and read by `deck-surface.js`. The sidecar contract needs it. No other bridge has a draw.\n- Both Dearborn match records stay `matches`, with the rise recorded as an `owner ruling` difference. Both side-by-sides are re-rendered.\n- New liberty `L-dearborn-level-draw-3361` covers `draw_profile`. `L-dearborn-picture-profile-2375` gains a withdrawal note.\n- `changelog.d/T-3361.json`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `tools/check.sh` is green on all four parts, with no untagged FAIL lines.\n- Desktop and 390x780 in-app before/after shots, with zero page errors, are in the project folder `drawbridge-level-T-3361/`. The draw reads level from the oblique, from the river side and on the deck.\n- Mobile smoke stages 1-4 and desktop stage 3 are running against the published mirror. The result follows in a comment.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01YWBQdZnEJErcfe6Uw2d1Gg)_",
